184-L186","doc":"The word of a normal form: its blocks, in order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.descRun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.descRun","kind":"def","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L178-L182","doc":"`descRun i j = [i, i-1, …, j]` — the descending run one block contributes.\nEvery intermediate value is a valid `Fin m` because `i` is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.elems","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.elems","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L172-L176","doc":"The elements of `s` in increasing order. `List.finRange` is already sorted,\nso no sorting algorithm is needed — and unlike `Finset.sort` this **reduces in\nthe kernel**, which is what makes every `decide` in this file possible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_six","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L165-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_five","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L159-L162","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_four","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L153-L156","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_three","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L147-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_two","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L142-L145","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_one","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L137-L140","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_zero","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L132-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.instFintypeNormalIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.instFintypeNormalIdx","kind":"instance","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.instDecidableEqNormalIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.instDecidableEqNormalIdx","kind":"instance","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.NormalIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.NormalIdx","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L114-L122","doc":"A Jones normal form for `TL_{m+1}(δ)`, as a pair of equal-size subsets of\nthe `m` generators with `J` dominating `I`.\n\nThe domination is stated as a threshold count rather than pointwise on sorted\nlists, which is what keeps the whole type decidable. ","signatureChunk":0}]}